    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "3624551b4552038097b91ef2cf67ad66793813def5e8524da223fb4e2a3f2a0c",
      "text": "After breakfast, visit the ruins of Palenque, considered among the most important Mayan archaeological sites in Mexico. The ancient city is nestled among jungle-covered hills. In the early morning, the ruins are often shrouded in mist, with small streams nearby, and the roar of jaguars or howler monkeys can sometimes be heard. The combination of nature and ancient ruins gives this place a special energy. Your guide will tell you the legends and stories of this mysterious city.\n\nThen, transfer to the colonial city of Campeche. Walk through narrow colonial streets and see the authentic city walls, which withstood numerous pirate attacks. Check-in at a 4* hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1NxdGb-AAzfs475TFliH1HR4SZCs03cmP",
